														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2425546">
									

<p>An excellent example of 'WTF have I just read?'. In a good way, I hasten to add!</p>
<p>Fun facts:</p>
<ul>
<li>when I saw the picture/read the 'mask attached to his face' part, I immediately thought: 'Where is my Mommy?' (<em>Doctor Who</em>, series 1 episode 9, <em>The Empty Child</em>) ;&gt;</li>
<li>a few paragraphs later, I thought: 'is this an allegory for the cause of global warming?'</li>
</ul>
<p>A few things that need to be clarified, IMO:<br />
- when SCP-2328 was found, was he already packed up in suit and mask?<br />
- is he really the son of Robert Vershinski? If he is, why is he described as <em>a construct resembling a Caucasian male human</em>? Also, why write <em>with no known living relatives</em> if Vershinski had a son?<br />
I do believe SCP-2328 is not Vershinski's son, but&#8230; not clear enough. I think it would be good to mention somewhere, for instance, that the Foundation tried to get him out of his suit and had to give up, because he's <span style="text-decoration: underline;">not</span> actually a man in a suit.</p>
<p>Still, all in all, a very good, original take on compulsive hoarding. Aaaaaand yes, upvote!</p>

